==German==

===Etymology===
Compound of {{affix|de|Tinte|t1=ink|-n-|Fisch|t3=fish}}.
Attested from the 17th century, as ''dinten Fisch'', equated with ''Merspin'' "sea-spider" in Joseph Du Chesne, Johann Adolph Ringelstein ''Diaeteticon polyhistoricum'' (1625). [http://books.google.com/books?id=gTlCAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA262&dq=Tintenfisch&hl=en&ei=p7s1TKLpH4-jOOTl3aEE&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CCsQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=Tintenfisch&f=false p. 218]

Glossed as synonymous with ''[[sepia]]'' ([[cuttlefish]]) in Tilesius, ''Verzeichnis verschiedener Fische und Krebse des adriatischen Meerbusens'' (1796), [http://books.google.com/books?id=MKQ-AAAAcAAJ&pg=PA45&dq=Tintenfisch&hl=en&ei=Zbs1TIveDcWIOObN8NIE&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CCsQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=Tintenfisch&f=false p. 45] and in Samuel Schilling, ''Ausführliche Naturgeschichte des Thier-, Pflanzen- und Mineralreichs'' vol. 3 (1839), [http://books.google.com/books?id=YJ85AAAAcAAJ&pg=PA135&dq=Tintenfisch&hl=en&ei=U7s1TI2hDouUOODttMkE&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CCYQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=Tintenfisch&f=false p. 134].

Later extended to other members of Coleoidea. Glossed as synonymous with ''[[Octopus]]'' in ''Globus'' vol. 61 (1892), [http://books.google.com/books?id=qKDlAAAAMAAJ&q=Tintenfisch&dq=Tintenfisch&hl=en&ei=w7o1TOXnI4OlOOOGlbEE&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CDcQ6AEwBA p. 195].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɪntn̩ˌfɪʃ/|/ˈtɪntənˌfɪʃ/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Tintenfisches|gen2=Tintenfischs|Tintenfische}}

# any member of the [[Coleoidea]] subclass of cephalopods; more specifically of [[cuttlefish]], but also of species of [[octopus|octopus]], [[squid]] etc.

====Usage notes====
* German-speakers without special knowledge of marine biology usually make no distinction between cuttlefish, octopus, and squid, calling all of them {{m|de||Tintenfisch}} and making this word a synonym of the less common {{m|de|Oktopus}}.

